- op: discuss  # 90bc
  at: '2026-04-17T17:08:35Z'  # 90bc
  by: agent  # 90bc
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 90bc
  clock: 3  # 90bc
  nonce: 90bc  # 90bc
  message: "Closing: misread the selector/dedup architecture. The selector is designed to cast wide (including permanently-relevant playbooks); dedup is designed to narrow (since the agent already has them in context). Novel picks break through precisely because they are novel. Pre-filtering 'skip these permanent picks' from the selector prompt would either require hand-curating which playbooks are 'permanent' (brittle), or would suppress exactly the novelty signal we want to preserve. The high dedup rate (~85%) is a selectivity signal, not waste. No infra change warranted."  # 90bc
